  "note": "Names on this page are printed surname first and are kept that way, as printed. Two centred columns, split at offset 100; the columns wander between offsets 44 and 70 on the left and 107 and 121 on the right, so the split is by which side of the page a run sits on rather than by a fixed offset. On line 16 the role 'DH' is printed at offset 90, still in the left half, and belongs to 'Cavaioli, Sue' on that line. school is recorded as 'high' because the bulk of the page is the high school's academic departments (English, Foreign Language, History, Math, Science, Unified Arts: High School) together with its guidance, athletics, library and special education. The page is NOT purely high school: the administration block names both the HS and the MS principal and secretary, and the last two blocks are 'Guidance: Middle School' and 'Specialists: Middle School', which continue onto page 128. A single school value cannot carry that; the grade_or_dept of each entry says which. Where a parenthesis encloses the whole of a role it is stripped ('Garamy, Alicia (Speech)' gives 'Speech'); where it does not, the text is kept as printed ('(10-12) DH', '(Music) MS'). Line 18 right column prints 'Hausler, Bradford b'; the trailing 'b' is recorded as role_raw but is most likely extraction noise -- no other entry on the page carries a single-letter role. Line 36 left column prints 'Brad McNamara & Hank' and is recorded as two entries; 'Hank' is a first name with no surname printed."
